  "description": "Learn essential vocabulary for professions, school life, and office environments in Korean.",
  "guidebook": "Welcome to **Work & School**! Here are two essential grammar tips for this unit:\n\n### 1. Locations: -에 vs. -에서\nBoth particles indicate locations, but in different ways:\n- Use **-에** with movement verbs like `가다` (to go) or existence verbs like `있다` (to be/exist): *학교에 가요* (\"I go to school\").\n- Use **-에서** when a specific action happens at a location: *사무실에서 일해요* (\"I work at the office\").\n\n### 2. Respectful Suffix: -님\nIn Korean, respecting professionals and seniors is vital. The suffix **-님** (nim) attaches to professions to show politeness, turning *선생* into *선생님* (teacher). Always address teachers with this honorific!",
